{"id":"CVE-2006-0733","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2006-02-16T11:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T16:48:55.786Z","description":"Cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability in WordPress 2.0.0 allows remote attackers to inject arbitrary web script or HTML via scriptable attributes such as (1) onfocus and (2) onblur in the \"author's website\" field.  NOTE: followup comments to the researcher's web log suggest that this issue is only exploitable by the same user who injects the XSS, so this might not be a vulnerability","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://myimei.com/security/2006-02-15/wordpress200autors-websitexss-attack.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/24736","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"wordpress-authorswebsite-xss(24736)"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/archive/1/425043/100/0/threaded","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20060214 [myimei]WordPress2.0.0~autors?website~XSS attack"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/16656","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"16656"}],"exploitdb":[{"edb":"27227","title":"WordPress Core 2.0 - Comment Post HTML Injection","type":"webapps","platform":"php","date":"2006-02-15","verified":"1"}],"vendors":["wordpress"]}
{"id":"CVE-2006-0985","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2006-03-03T11:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T16:56:14.846Z","description":"Multiple cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities in the \"post comment\" functionality of WordPress 2.0.1 and earlier allow remote attackers to inject arbitrary web script or HTML via the (1) name, (2) website, and (3) comment parameters.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/24957","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"wordpress-wpcommentspost-xss(24957)"},{"url":"http://NeoSecurityTeam.net/advisories/Advisory-17.txt","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/19050","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"19050"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/archive/1/426304/100/0/threaded","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20060227 WordPress 2.0.1 Multiple Vulnerabilities"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2006/0777","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2006-0777"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/archive/1/426574/100/0/threaded","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20060302 Re: FW: WordPress 2.0.1 Multiple Vulnerabilities"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/archive/1/426504/100/0/threaded","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20060228 FW: WordPress 2.0.1 Multiple Vulnerabilities"}],"vendors":["wordpress"]}
{"id":"CVE-2006-0986","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2006-03-03T11:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T16:56:15.264Z","description":"WordPress 2.0.1 and earlier allows remote attackers to obtain sensitive information via a direct request to (1) default-filters.php, (2) template-loader.php, (3) rss-functions.php, (4) locale.php, (5) wp-db.php, and (6) kses.php in the wp-includes/ directory; and (7) edit-form-advanced.php, (8) admin-functions.php, (9) edit-link-form.php, (10) edit-page-form.php, (11) admin-footer.php, and (12) menu.php in the wp-admin directory; and possibly (13) list directory contents of the wp-includes directory.  NOTE: the vars.php, edit-form.php, wp-settings.php, and edit-form-comment.php vectors are already covered by CVE-2005-4463.  The menu-header.php vector is already covered by CVE-2005-2110.  Other vectors might be covered by CVE-2005-1688.  NOTE: if the typical installation of WordPress does not list any site-specific files to wp-includes, then vector [13] is not an exposure.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://NeoSecurityTeam.net/advisories/Advisory-17.txt","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/19050","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"19050"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/archive/1/426304/100/0/threaded","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20060227 WordPress 2.0.1 Multiple Vulnerabilities"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2006/0777","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2006-0777"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/archive/1/426574/100/0/threaded","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20060302 Re: FW: WordPress 2.0.1 Multiple Vulnerabilities"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/archive/1/426504/100/0/threaded","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20060228 FW: WordPress 2.0.1 Multiple Vulnerabilities"}],"vendors":["wordpress"]}
